  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of the inadequate provision and poor quality of communal amenity space, the failure to demonstrate compliance with minimum internal residential quality standards, and the contrived design of the proposed third-floor accommodation, including its reliance on rooflights as the sole source of daylight, sunlight, outlook and ventilation, would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers. The proposal would therefore represent an overly intensive form of development contrary to Policies D6 and D13 of the London Plan (2021), Policies SC5, SC7, CC1 and CC2 of the Hounslow Local Plan, the Council's Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD, and the objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the proposal can adequately accommodate the additional parking demand arising from the proposed residential intensification, or that the existing parking provision and surrounding highway network have sufficient capacity to do so without resulting in unacceptable parking stress. In the absence of a robust parking survey in the surrounding area, parking occupancy data within the site, how the existing spaces are allocated, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the development would not adversely affect the safe and efficient operation of the highway network. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy T6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy EC2 of the Hounslow Local Plan."
  ],
